  "intro": "The 6 OpenTelemetry metrics OpenCTI 7.260309.0-lts.8 exposes to monitor a deployment, with the attributes each data point carries. Turn them on and collect them as [Metrics](/deploy/operate/metrics/) explains.",
  "filter": "Filter metrics and attributes",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Observability metrics",
      "text": "The platform exports these metrics when `app:telemetry:metrics:enabled` is `true`, to an OTLP endpoint (`app:telemetry:metrics:exporter_otlp`) or on a Prometheus port (`app:telemetry:metrics:exporter_prometheus`). It also exports the Node.js runtime metrics of the `opentelemetry-node-metrics` library, with no prefix: their names come from the library, not from the OpenCTI code.",
      "columns": [
        "Metric",
        "Kind",
        "Unit",
        "Description",
        "Attributes"
      ],
